==================================================
2. BUILD STAGE 4
==================================================

Primary stage:

Stage 4 — Structure & Isomerism

Learning progression should cover, at minimum:

A. Molecular Structure
- molecular formula vs structural representation
- connectivity
- bond arrangement

B. Constitutional Isomerism
- same molecular formula
- different connectivity
- visual comparison

C. Structure Comparison
- compare two molecules side-by-side
- highlight changed connectivity
- explain why they are/are not isomers

D. Basic Stereochemical Awareness
- introduce spatial arrangement visually where appropriate
- avoid pretending to provide advanced stereochemistry if the deterministic model does not support it
- use a constrained, reliable representation rather than fake 3D chemistry

E. Challenge / Assessment
- identify structural relationships
- construct a valid isomer
- distinguish identical molecule vs isomer
- detect invalid structures
- justify an answer through structured interaction and/or short response

